From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Consume a complete quartet at the input boundary
License: MIT
Upstream-Status: Not submitted (no upstream writes)

Portable decoder defect, not an architecture-specific claim. With four
encoded wchar_t values (two input bytes), the loop fills state->i to four
and exhausts input. Returning immediately leaves an invalid quartet for
blockend, which permits only zero or two trailing values. Consume it now;
keep incomplete quartets buffered. CI tests exercise exact two-byte input
and chunk widths one through thirteen against the actual shared library.
No test, public-domain notice, default target or feature is removed.

diff --git a/src/cdecode.c b/src/cdecode.c
--- a/src/cdecode.c
+++ b/src/cdecode.c
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ ptrdiff_t rcnb_decode_block(const wchar_t* code_in, size_t length_in,
         length_in--;
         code_in++;
     }
-    if (length_in == 0)
+    if (length_in == 0 && state_in->i < 4)
         return 0;
     res = rcnb_decode_short(state_in->trailing_code, &plaintext_char);
     if (!res)
